    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="d210-02" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve05p1/d210-02"/>

                <head>211. Letter From President Nixon to Major General Gowon<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d211-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d211-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1971-10-29"
                        >October 29, 1971</date>
                </dateline>
                <pb facs="d211-01" n="1" xml:id="d211-01"/>
                <p>Dear General Gowon:</p>
                <p>Thank you for your kind letter of September 18 explaining the urgent concerns in
                    Nigeria and Africa which rule out for the present your undertaking a journey to
                    the United States. I have looked forward to our meeting and genuinely regret its
                    postponement. At the same time, however, I am encouraged by the ongoing success
                    of your Governmentʼs policies at home and the broadening scope of your personal
                    involvement in decisions affecting peace and prosperity in Africa. In these
                    endeavors, you have my continuin support and my warmest wishes for success. I
                    want to assure you that my invitation remains open, and I hope that, as our
                    respective commitments for next year become clearer, it will be possible to find
                    a mutually convenient time for our meeting.</p>
                <closer>Sincerely, <signed>Richard M. Nixon</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d211-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d211-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Presidential
                    Correspondence, 1969–1974, Nigeria-Gen. Gowon. No classification marking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d211-f2" n="2" xml:id="d211-f2-content">
                <p> Nixon responded to Gowonʼs September 18 letter, regretting that a visit was not
                    possible, but holding the invitation open for 1972.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
